From: Maxime <maxime.lefrancois@emse.fr>
Date: Fri, 27 Nov 2026 09:57:45 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 6/6] Reference-valued IRI term maps: the value as is, not
 percent-encoded

R2RML and RML-Core percent-encode only the values inserted in a template.
A reference with the term type IRI gives its value as is, resolved against
the base IRI when it is relative: `https://www.crtm.es/billetes-y-tarifas`
gave `<https:%2F%2Fwww.crtm.es%2Fbilletes-y-tarifas>` (GTFS-Madrid-Bench,
agency_fare_url), and `Bob/Charles` gave `<http://example.com/base/Bob%2FCharles>`
(RMLTC0020b without @base).

Objects and subjects of CSV, JSON, XML, MySQL and PostgreSQL sources; templates
and blank nodes keep their encoding. Test: rdfizer/tests/test_reference_iri.py.
